# Provenance

Ported from LIMSOC Permission Assist, `host/src`, at `origin/main` commit `efc934f`, obtained with `git archive origin/main` into a scratch directory. That repository was read only; nothing was branched or committed there.

| This package | Source | How |
|---|---|---|
| `src/safe-redirect.ts` | `host/src/lib/safe-redirect.ts` | Verbatim |
| `src/csp.ts` `inlineScriptHashes`, `SITE_HEADERS` | `host/src/lib/site.ts` | Verbatim |
| `src/csp.ts` `buildCsp` | `host/src/lib/site.ts` | Changed: `connect-src 'self'` (bridge calls to own host), `worker-src 'self' blob:`, `form-action 'self'`. Still no external origin |
| `src/csp.ts` `BASE_SECURITY_HEADERS` | `host/next.config.ts` `headers()` | Verbatim values |
| `src/session.ts` sign and verify | `host/src/lib/auth.ts` `signOtpSession` / `verifyOtpSessionCookie` | Rewritten around the same HMAC-SHA256, base64url, timing-safe compare; payload gains `app` and `role`; prefix `poc1` |
| `src/session.ts` cookie flags | `host/src/lib/auth.ts` `sessionCookieOptions` | Same name `__session`, 14 days, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in production, Path=/ |
| `src/exchange.ts` | `host/src/app/api/auth/session/route.ts` | Rewritten: allow-list lookup replaced by the `poc_<appId>` claim; Web `Request`/`Response`; structured refusal logs |
| `src/rate-limit.ts` | `host/src/lib/rate-limit.ts` | Rewritten: injectable store; `getClientIp` counts from the right of `X-Forwarded-For` instead of trusting the first hop |
| `src/firebase.ts` | `host/src/lib/firebase-admin.ts`, rate-limit transaction | Changed: named database, ADC only, no Auth admin calls |
| `src/claims.ts` | Service Summary `src/lib/claims.ts` (`bf5f88c`) | Same contract (`poc_<id>` = "member" or "admin"); adds `withAppClaim` which merges instead of replacing |

New here: `src/access.ts` (per-request gate with the hub's access override), `src/log.ts`.

## Why POC hosts do not use Firebase session cookies

Permission Assist creates and revocation-checks Firebase session cookies, which needs `roles/firebaseauth.admin` at project level. In the shared project that role would let any POC grant itself another POC's claim. So only the hub holds it. POC hosts verify the ID token once (Google's public keys, no IAM), sign their own `__session` cookie with a per-app secret, and learn about revokes and downgra
